  "reply_to_counterargument": "I accept the causal objection: correlated post-description ratings do not establish independent pathways, and my previous ranking gave insufficient priority to legitimacy as a prerequisite for usefulness. I therefore promote the serial account into the leading pair. I retain parallel pathways as a live rival because descriptions can directly convey task applications as well as organizational appropriateness; this is a theoretical possibility, not empirical support. The falsifiable dispute is whether randomized framing still changes usefulness when legitimacy is genuinely fixed, and whether it still changes interest when usefulness is genuinely fixed.",
  "changes_or_reason_for_no_change": "The strongest two rivals are now parallel authorization/application and legitimacy-gated usefulness; usefulness-only moves to third. Legitimacy-only is deprioritized because it omits instrumental valuation, although it could fit appropriateness-driven decisions. Reverse usefulness-to-legitimacy ordering, direct framing effects, and response-demand explanations remain possible but are less specifically motivated here, not disproven. I will not treat baseline mediation regressions as resolving the challenge. No evidence has yet been supplied.",
  "remaining_uncertainty": "The interventions must fix psychological states rather than merely overwrite recorded scores, and must not introduce additional routes to interest. Zero may be a special boundary condition: an apparent blocked pathway could reflect an interaction rather than serial ordering. Separate evaluations may differ in populations or procedures. Null effects can reflect imprecision or cancellation, and surviving effects would reject restrictive graphs without identifying a unique replacement. Measured technical fit and quality cannot safely be treated as pre-description moderators unless their timing is established. Simulated expressed interest is not actual procurement or adoption.",
  "contrasting_predictions": "Freeze before evidence: In a setting where the proposed positive pathways are active, the parallel account predicts positive X effects on V and Y with L fixed at zero, and a positive X effect on Y with V fixed at zero. The strict serial account predicts zero X effects on both V and Y with L fixed, and zero X effect on Y but a preserved X effect on L with V fixed. The usefulness-only account predicts positive X effects on V and Y with L fixed, but zero X effect on Y with V fixed. All three allow positive baseline effects on L, V, and Y, so baseline correlations cannot distinguish them. A surviving X effect on V under fixed L contradicts strict serial gating; a surviving X effect on Y under fixed V contradicts both restrictive usefulness-mediated accounts, subject to intervention validity. Failure to detect an effect is not evidence of an exact zero without adequate precision.",
  "requests": [
    "Using the baseline and legitimacy-fixed-at-zero evaluations, estimate relational-minus-attribute-bound differences in usefulness, adoption interest, and legitimacy separately within each dataset, with uncertainty intervals. Report the fixed legitimacy distribution as an implementation check. Show cross-dataset differences in the usefulness and interest effects, but distinguish randomized within-dataset effects from comparisons across separate evaluations. From existing documentation, report whether fixing legitimacy changed the psychological state or only the recorded score, and whether recruitment and procedures were comparable. Do not condition on measured post-description mediators.",
    "Using the usefulness-fixed-at-zero evaluation, estimate relational-minus-attribute-bound differences in adoption interest and legitimacy, with uncertainty intervals, and report the usefulness distribution as an implementation check. Compare these effects with the corresponding baseline estimates from the first analysis, clearly noting that cross-evaluation contrasts are not automatically randomized. From existing documentation, assess whether usefulness was psychologically fixed and whether other procedures changed. Report effect sizes and precision rather than using nonsignificance alone to declare a pathway absent."
